<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Landgraviate of Hesse-Homburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1622 CE – 1866 CE · capital Bad Homburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Hessian landgraviate in the Taunus, home of the soldier-prince of Kleist's drama and later of a celebrated spa and casino.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Hesse-Homburg was established in 1622 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-v-landgrave-of-hesse-darmstadt">Landgrave Louis V</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Hesse-Darmstadt</a> granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-homburg-vor-der-hohe">Homburg vor der Höhe</a> to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-landgrave-of-hesse-homburg">Frederick I</a> as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a>. It remained dependent on Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> for most of its history rather than a fully sovereign state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Frederick II, who lost a leg in Swedish service and commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> cavalry at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fehrbellin">Fehrbellin</a> in 1675, built the baroque palace and inspired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-von-kleist">Heinrich von Kleist's</a> play <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-prince-of-homburg">The Prince of Homburg</a>. Later landgraves welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenot</a> and Waldensian refugees. In the 19th century Homburg grew into a fashionable spa, and its casino, opened in 1841, drew visitors from across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Hesse-Homburg was mediatised to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Hesse-Darmstadt</a> in 1806 but restored as a sovereign member of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a> in 1815, gaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meisenheim">Meisenheim</a>. The line died out in 1866, the lands passed briefly to the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> and were then annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/landgraviate-of-hesse-homburg.jpg" alt="Landgraviate of Hesse-Homburg" width="300" height="200"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hesse-Homburg.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1622 CE – 1866 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bad Homburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Frederick I, Frederick II, Frederick V</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Calvinism, Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hessen-Homburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1744&amp;focus=landgraviate-of-hesse-homburg" aria-label="Landgraviate of Hesse-Homburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4877 432 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Landgraviate of Hesse-Homburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5197 688L5198 698M5197 688L5199 691M5197 688L5198 698"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5198 698h0M5199 691h0M5198 698h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5197 688h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5197 688h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1744&amp;focus=landgraviate-of-hesse-homburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
